  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Towards 100% renewable energy cities and regions for climate change mitigation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The use of renewable energies (RE) as well as achieving local improvements to energy efficiency are both key aspects of climate change mitigation. The project supported cities and regions in partner countries in efforts to develop strategies for sourcing 100 percent of their energy needs from renewables. It was also helping relevant stakeholders to engage in the deployment of renewable energy sources and assessed local potential for renewables, created implementation models and helped promising projects to raise financing. The project also initiated a dialogue between the various levels of government, strengthened expertise in the renewables field and encouraged the development of suitable framework at the national, regional and local level. In this way, the project promoted the expansion of renewables energies and improved energy efficiency.</narrative>
  </description>
